# Titles and descriptions of the commands (blueprint 10.1). Quick search and the CLI show them.

command-projects-list-title = Show projects
command-projects-list-description = Lists the registered projects with their newest scan.
command-projects-add-title = Add project
command-projects-add-description = Registers a folder or a Git repository as a project and scans it.
command-projects-rescan-title = Scan project again
command-projects-rescan-description = Scans a project again; only changed files are read if it was scanned before, unless a full scan is asked for.
command-tools-indexers-title = List indexers
command-tools-indexers-description = Checks which indexers of level 2 are installed on this computer: where each one was found, its version and, if it does not work, the line of its error. Starts only version queries, never project code, and needs no project.
command-projects-tools-title = Check tools
command-projects-tools-description = Checks which tools level 2 needs for the languages of a project, whether they are installed and new enough, and stores the result. Starts only version queries, never project code.
command-projects-cancel-title = Cancel scan
command-projects-cancel-description = Stops the running scan of a project at the next stage boundary; no snapshot is written.
command-projects-rename-title = Rename project
command-projects-rename-description = Gives a project another display name. The folder or Git address, the number and all scans stay as they are. An empty name goes back to the name that the source suggests.
command-projects-suggest-name-title = Suggest project name
command-projects-suggest-name-description = Tells the name that a folder or Git address would get as a project, so the form can show it before the project is added.
command-projects-remove-title = Remove project
command-projects-remove-description = Removes a project and everything stored about it (scans, level 2 consent, tool reports, notes) from the app. The files of the project and the stored logins stay untouched.
command-projects-folder-dialog-title = Check folder dialog
command-projects-folder-dialog-description = Tells whether an operating system folder dialog can be shown on this machine.
command-projects-pick-folder-title = Pick folder
command-projects-pick-folder-description = Shows the operating system folder dialog on the machine of the app and returns the chosen path, or none if it was cancelled. Nothing is read or created in the folder.
command-explorer-outline-title = Show structure
command-explorer-outline-description = Lists the layers, namespaces and types of the newest scan.
command-explorer-symbol-title = Show symbol
command-explorer-symbol-description = Shows one type or member with its metrics and members.
command-search-query-title = Search symbols
command-search-query-description = Searches the names of the types and members of the newest scan.
command-status-info-title = Show status
command-status-info-description = Shows the version, the start time and the memory of the program.
command-explorer-source-title = Show source
command-explorer-source-description = Shows the lines of the declaration of a type or member, read from the project folder.
command-usages-query-title = Show usages
command-usages-query-description = Lists who uses a symbol, what it uses and what a change of it reaches, with the certainty of each reference.
command-usages-code-title = Show the code of the hits
command-usages-code-description = Returns the code lines of the hits of a usages query, read from the project folder.
command-graph-layers-title = Show dependency map
command-graph-layers-description = Places the layers of the newest scan and the dependencies between them for the dependency map.
command-export-html-title = Export as HTML
command-export-html-description = Writes the explorer, the dependency map and the usages of the newest scan into one self-contained HTML page. The source code is not part of it.
command-credentials-list-title = Show credentials
command-credentials-list-description = Lists the credentials that Git projects log in with and whether each is stored. Never shows a secret.
command-credentials-set-title = Save credential
command-credentials-set-description = Stores or replaces the login of a Git source in the keystore of the system. The secret is only sent here and never returned.
command-credentials-delete-title = Remove credential
command-credentials-delete-description = Removes a stored login from the keystore of the system.
command-preferences-get-title = Show preferences
command-preferences-get-description = Shows the theme and the language the user has chosen for the UI.
command-preferences-set-title = Save preferences
command-preferences-set-description = Saves the theme and the language of the UI, so that every browser of the user shows them.
command-ui-settings-get-title = Show saved settings
command-ui-settings-get-description = Shows the settings the UI saved in the data folder, for now the memory limit per indexer.
command-ui-settings-set-indexer-memory-title = Save memory limit of an indexer
command-ui-settings-set-indexer-memory-description = Saves or forgets the memory limit in MB of one indexer for level 2. The value counts from the next scan and lies between the user file and the project file.
command-rules-show-title = Show rules
command-rules-show-description = Shows the architecture rules of a project from its `.codeskimr.toml` with their violations down to the place in the code, and marks held old burdens.
command-unused-keep-title = Keep a symbol on purpose
command-unused-keep-description = Writes an entry into the exception list `[[unused.ignore]]` of the `.codeskimr.toml` of a folder project, so that the symbol is no longer counted as unused.
command-unused-lift-title = Lift an exception
command-unused-lift-description = Takes an entry out of the exception list `[[unused.ignore]]` of a folder project, so that its symbols count as unused again.
command-layers-get-title = Show layers
command-layers-get-description = Shows the layers a project has set and the namespaces of the last scan that layers can be built from.
command-layers-set-title = Save layers
command-layers-set-description = Writes the layers of a folder project into its `.codeskimr.toml`; they apply from the next scan.
command-annotations-list-title = List annotations
command-annotations-list-description = Lists the critical marks, notes and tasks of a project, filtered by symbol, kind and status, one page at a time.
command-annotations-summary-title = Count annotations per symbol
command-annotations-summary-description = Returns for each annotated symbol of a project whether it is critical and how many notes and tasks it has, so that trees and tables can show marks and counters.
command-annotations-create-title = Add annotation
command-annotations-create-description = Adds a critical mark, a note or a task to a namespace, type or member.
command-annotations-mark-critical-title = Mark as critical
command-annotations-mark-critical-description = Marks a symbol as system critical; a later change of it raises an alert.
command-annotations-add-note-title = Add note
command-annotations-add-note-description = Writes a note on a namespace, type or member.
command-annotations-add-task-title = Add task
command-annotations-add-task-description = Creates a task on a namespace, type or member, with an optional due date and assignee.
command-annotations-update-title = Change annotation
command-annotations-update-description = Changes the text, the status, the due date or the assignee of an annotation, or assigns it to another symbol when its own symbol is gone.
command-annotations-delete-title = Remove annotation
command-annotations-delete-description = Deletes an annotation together with its baseline and its alerts.
command-alerts-list-title = List alerts
command-alerts-list-description = Lists the alerts of critical symbols that changed, were removed or lost their place, newest first, one page at a time.
command-alerts-dismiss-title = Dismiss alert
command-alerts-dismiss-description = Removes one alert from the open list; the symbol as it is now becomes its baseline.
command-alerts-dismiss-all-title = Dismiss all alerts
command-alerts-dismiss-all-description = Removes every open alert that matches the filter. It needs the explicit confirmation flag.
command-level2-status-title = Show level 2 state
command-level2-status-description = Shows whether level 2 is switched on for a project, whether it is confirmed and whether the server can open the confirmation window or the screen has to show the command. Returns no path and no text of the project.
command-level2-revoke-title = Switch level 2 off
command-level2-revoke-description = Takes the confirmation of level 2 back for a project, as `codeskimr level2 revoke` does. Stored results stay until the next scan; a running indexer ends within its limits.
command-scans-list-title = List the last scans
command-scans-list-description = Lists the scans of a project that are kept, newest first, with the time, the kind, the duration, the number of files and the number of files each scan changed.
command-stats-overview-title = Show statistics
command-stats-overview-description = Summarises the newest scan of a project: usages, symbols without usages, complexity and the first rows of every ranking.
command-stats-ranking-title = Show a ranking
command-stats-ranking-description = Ranks the symbols of the newest scan: the most used, those without a usage found, the most complex, the largest and the most coupled.
command-settings-effective-title = Show effective settings
command-settings-effective-description = Shows every setting as it holds now: its value and where the value comes from (default, configuration file or command line). Secret values are never shown, and nothing can be changed here.
command-scope-get-title = Show scope of project
command-scope-get-description = Shows which languages and folders a project covers and which it leaves out, with the number of files of each, counted in the folder as a scan would walk it.
command-scope-set-title = Set scope of project
command-scope-set-description = Stores the languages and folders that the scans of a project leave out. The change applies from the next scan; the code stays one project.
command-rename-preview-title = Check a rename
command-rename-preview-description = Shows the places, name conflicts and text hits that a new name for a symbol would hit. Nothing is changed.
command-graph-modules-title = Show modules and cycles
command-graph-modules-description = Shows the modules of the newest scan with coupling and stability, the cycles between them with a suggestion how to end them, and modules that stand out.
